{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Clean BSE-NSE Ticker Data for Earnings Season Tracker",
  "scenario": "Your coverage desk has received a raw CSV export from the BSE announcement page with 12 listed companies, their result-announcement dates, and stock prices. The data arrives with invisible spaces, mixed case, text-formatted numbers, and dates in ambiguous DD/MM format. You must clean this pipeline in helper columns to build a working earnings-season countdown tracker.",
  "instructions": "Build a six-station cleaning pipeline in columns D–I: TRIM the tickers, extract the company codes via FIND–LEFT, convert names to proper case, turn text-prices into numbers, parse dates correctly, and calculate days until each announcement. Answer the summary questions in column B of the Answers sheet.",
  "learning_objective": "Apply TRIM, LEFT, FIND, PROPER, VALUE, EOMONTH and date arithmetic to rescue messy market data and build a self-updating results calendar.",
  "hints": [
    "Station 1: Every cleaning pipeline begins with TRIM. In D2, write =TRIM(A2) to kill invisible leading and trailing spaces.",
    "Station 2: Use FIND to locate the dot in the ticker, then LEFT to grab everything before it. The formula is =LEFT(D2, FIND(\".\", D2) - 1). The −1 means 'stop one character short of the dot.'",
    "Station 5: Text that looks like numbers won't SUM or sort right. Convert via =VALUE(G2) in column H, or use the shortcut =--G2 inside a bigger formula. Then verify the result is right-aligned, not left."
  ],
